      "date": "",
      "content": "Social Media Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Rss Podcast whatsapp Download Mobile App Language Selection Menu Listen News Midday News Mann Ki Baat Screen Reader Access Transcript summary Play Audio Midday News News On AIR | August 9, 2026 2:01 PM Home Minister Amit Shah says, 3 new criminal laws are aimed at providing time-bound justice through technology driven mechanism Union Home Minister Amit Shah said that the three new criminal laws introduced by the Modi Government, replacing the colonial-era laws, are based on three important pillars – technology, timeline and trust. Mr Shah said the objective of the new criminal laws is to ensure justice to citizens through a system that is more technology-driven and time-bound. The Home Minister was participating in the presentation ceremony of the President’s Police Colour to the Puducherry Police at the Police Training School ground in Gorimedu. Later today, he will flag off a Har Ghar Tiranga Yatra at Muruga Theatre Signal in Puducherry. Congratulating the Puducherry Police, Mr. Amit Shah said that receiving the President’s Police Colour is one of the most glorious moments in the life of any disciplined police force. He said that although the Puducherry Police has a strength of less than 5,000 personnel, it is entrusted with protecting Puducherry, maintaining its internal security and safeguarding the honour and dignity of the Union Territory, which has a rich spiritual heritage. With this historic recognition of the President’s Police Colour, Puducherry has become the 18th State/Union Territory in the country to be bestowed with this highest honour conferred upon a police force. Puducherry Lieutenant Governor K. Kailashnathan, Chief Minister N. Rangasamy, Home Minister A. Namassivayam and Director General of Police Shalini Singh were also present on the occasion. Most Read View All 6 hours ago 376 PM Narendra Modi and US Vice-Prez JD Vance discuss ways to further strengthen Comprehen... 6 hours ago 260 Har Ghar Tiranga campaign begins today, coinciding with 150th anniversary of India’s Na... 6 hours ago 242 Amarnath Yatra to remain suspended from both Pahalgam and Baltal routes 4 hours ago 234 Pentagon orders US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries 6 hours ago 181 Appointment of 30 Judges for High Courts of Madras, Calcutta, Madhya Pradesh and Karnat... Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved Last Updated: 9th Aug 2026 Back to top",
