      "content": "Social Media Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Rss Podcast whatsapp Download Mobile App Language Selection Menu Listen News Midday News Mann Ki Baat Screen Reader Access Transcript summary Play Audio Midday News News On AIR | August 9, 2026 1:46 PM China: Over 1,300 flights cancelled and 3 lakh people relocated ahead of Typhoon Dolphin In China, Shanghai’s two airports cancelled more than 1,300 flights and authorities relocated over 3 lakh people in surrounding regions as the country prepared for Typhoon Dolphin. The outer bands of the storm hit northern Taiwan yesterday, including the capital Taipei, bringing rain. Some Taiwanese airlines also cancelled their flights to China. The storm’s maximum sustained winds were estimated at about 162 kilometres per hour as of today morning. It is bringing heavy rains, creating a risk of severe flooding as well as landslides and is expected to hit Zhejiang province and northern parts of neighbouring Fujian province. Authorities are warning of severe landslide risks in Zhejiang. Shanghai’s Hongqiao and Pudong airports also cancelled about 60 per cent of expected flights. Authorities in Zhejiang evacuated some 3 lakh 90 thousand people in the city of Taizhou yesterday. Most Read View All 6 hours ago 376 PM Narendra Modi and US Vice-Prez JD Vance discuss ways to further strengthen Comprehen... 6 hours ago 260 Har Ghar Tiranga campaign begins today, coinciding with 150th anniversary of India’s Na... 6 hours ago 242 Amarnath Yatra to remain suspended from both Pahalgam and Baltal routes 4 hours ago 234 Pentagon orders US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries 6 hours ago 181 Appointment of 30 Judges for High Courts of Madras, Calcutta, Madhya Pradesh and Karnat... Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved Last Updated: 9th Aug 2026 Back to top",
