      "content": "Social Media Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Rss Podcast whatsapp Download Mobile App Language Selection Menu Listen News Midday News Mann Ki Baat Screen Reader Access Transcript summary Play Audio Midday News News On AIR | August 9, 2026 1:58 PM Ashmita Chaliha clinches her 1st BWF world tour title at Korea Masters 2026 Ashmita Chaliha. Indian shuttler Ashmita Chaliha produced a superb comeback to win the Korea Masters 2026, beating China’s Han Qian Xi in the women’s singles final this morning. The Assam shuttler recovered from losing the opening game to prevail 14-21, 21-14, and 21-14 in 53 minutes and claim her first BWF title. Earlier, Ashmita reached the final after defeating fellow Indian Rakshitha Ramraj 21-13, 16-21, 21-13 in the semifinal yesterday. While Han outplayed South Korea’s G Kim 22-20, 18-21, and 21-14 in the other semifinal to advance to the final. Ashmita Chaliha had won the gold medal at the 2024 Asia Team Championships. At the 2019 South Asian Games, she had secured gold medals in both the women’s singles and team events. Most Read View All 6 hours ago 376 PM Narendra Modi and US Vice-Prez JD Vance discuss ways to further strengthen Comprehen... 6 hours ago 260 Har Ghar Tiranga campaign begins today, coinciding with 150th anniversary of India’s Na... 6 hours ago 242 Amarnath Yatra to remain suspended from both Pahalgam and Baltal routes 4 hours ago 234 Pentagon orders US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries 6 hours ago 181 Appointment of 30 Judges for High Courts of Madras, Calcutta, Madhya Pradesh and Karnat... Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved Last Updated: 9th Aug 2026 Back to top",
