      "content": "Social Media Links Facebook Twitter Instagram YouTube Rss Podcast whatsapp Download Mobile App Language Selection Menu Listen News Midday News Mann Ki Baat Screen Reader Access Transcript summary Play Audio Midday News News On AIR | August 9, 2026 1:21 PM NBA disburses over 3 crore rupees under Access and Benefit Sharing mechanism to 33 States/UTs and National Institutes The National Biodiversity Authority (NBA) has disbursed over 3 crore rupees as Access and Benefit Sharing (ABS) to 33 State Biodiversity Boards, Union Territory Biodiversity Councils and National Institutes. The Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate Change said that the release covers a diverse range of India’s agrobiodiversity, including tomato, chilli, brinjal and deep-frozen Sahiwal cattle semen. It informed that cumulative ABS disbursements by the NBA have now exceeded 166 crore rupees. The Ministry also said that each release further strengthens the link between biodiversity conservation, scientific research and the livelihoods of the communities that conserve India’s rich biological resources. Most Read View All 6 hours ago 377 PM Narendra Modi and US Vice-Prez JD Vance discuss ways to further strengthen Comprehen... 6 hours ago 260 Har Ghar Tiranga campaign begins today, coinciding with 150th anniversary of India’s Na... 6 hours ago 242 Amarnath Yatra to remain suspended from both Pahalgam and Baltal routes 4 hours ago 234 Pentagon orders US defense companies to accelerate weapons production and deliveries 6 hours ago 182 Appointment of 30 Judges for High Courts of Madras, Calcutta, Madhya Pradesh and Karnat... Privacy Policy | Copyright © 2026 News On Air. All rights reserved Last Updated: 9th Aug 2026 Back to top",
